   "sentenceId": 13,
   "he": "רַבִּי יִשְׁמָעֵאל אוֹמֵר: אַרְבַּעְתָּן אַרְבַּע מִצְוֹת. אָמַר רַב יְהוּדָה אָמַר שְׁמוּאֵל: הֲלָכָה כְּרַבִּי יִשְׁמָעֵאל, וְלֵית הִלְכְתָא כְּוָתֵיהּ.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that «Rabbi Yishmael says: The four of them are four» discrete «mitzvot,» and the absence of one does not prevent fulfillment of the rest. «Rav Yehuda says» that «Shmuel says:» The «halakha» is «in accordance with» the opinion of «Rabbi Yishmael.» The Gemara states: «But the halakha» is «not in accordance with his» opinion."
